# Shared Components

Catalog and status of every component: `Docs/shared-components.md`. Preview them in the gallery
(`Views/Dev/GalleryView.axaml`, opened from the login screen in Debug builds).

## Reuse first
Before writing UI, use what exists (`xmlns:ui="using:Mostawsef.Desktop.Components"`):
- Layout: `AppShell`, `NavMenu`/`NavMenuItem`, `TopBar`, `BrandMark`, `PreferencesBar`, `PageHeader`, `Card`, `Section`, `Divider`, `ResponsiveGrid`, `PageHost`
- Forms: `FormField`, `SearchBox`, `PasswordField` (form grids: `ResponsiveGrid MaxColumns="2"` of `FormField`s)
- Buttons: `IconButton` (+ styled built-in `Button`, `SplitButton`, `DropDownButton`)
- Data: `DataTable` (wraps `DataGrid`), `Pagination`, `Badge`, `Avatar`, `StatCard`, `DetailsView`/`DetailsItem`
- Feedback/overlays: `Spinner`, `LoadingOverlay`, `EmptyState`, `ErrorState`, `Alert`, `Toast` (via `ToastService`), `Modal`, `ConfirmDialog`, `DialogHost`
- Built-in controls (TextBox, ComboBox, AutoCompleteBox, CalendarDatePicker, TabControl, ...) are already themed: use them directly.

## Deferred components
Chart, Timeline, Skeleton, Drawer, AppointmentCard, PrescriptionItem,
InvoiceSummary, VitalsDisplay are **not built**. Create one only when a screen needs it, and delete
components that no screen uses. Scheduler, Wizard/Stepper, Breadcrumb, ButtonGroup, ListDetailsView,
FormSection, ValidationSummary, DateRangePicker, FileUpload/ImagePicker, PatientCard/PatientHeader and
PrintPreview were removed while unused: restore from git history (commit `983d1b9`) when a screen needs one.
Pages that load data implement `ILoadablePage`: the shell reuses each menu page's view model for the portal lifetime
(`PageHost` caches the view per page instance and toggles `IsVisible` so DataGrids are not detached), calls `ActivateAsync` when it is shown and `Deactivate`
when the user leaves (cancels in-flight API calls; a cancelled first load marks the page stale so the next visit reloads).
New order and Order details use the same reuse pattern (`OrdersViewModel` holds each instance; reset via `BeginReuse()` / `Seed`).
Pass a cancellation token to every API read a page makes (`PagedListViewModel.ReadAsync` for one-off reads such as details).
List pages derive from `ViewModels/Shell/NumberedListViewModel` (page numbers; records sorted by a field, e.g. users) or
`PagedListViewModel` (cursor paging; append-only newest-first logs). Both expose the same bindings and keep rows in one
`ListPageItems<T>` instance (`ReplaceAll` on reload; `PrependNewest` after create when the new row can sit on page 1).
A failed load shows the `DataTable` error state (bind `HasError`, `ErrorTitle`/`ErrorDescription` via `{l:TrKey LoadError...Key}`
and `RetryCommand="{Binding RefreshCommand}"`). Use toasts for failed actions (save, delete), the error state for content
that could not load. Prefer `DataGridTextColumn` + `ValueConverters` for money/dates in tables; keep template columns for
badges, actions and `RowNumber`.

## Creating a component
1. Class in `Components/<Category>/<Name>.cs`, namespace `Mostawsef.Desktop.Components`.
   Expose `StyledProperty`s; use `DirectProperty` for read-only/computed values and internal commands.
2. `ControlTheme` keyed `{x:Type ui:Name}` in `Components/<Category>/<Category>Themes.axaml` (included from `Styles/Theme.axaml`).
   A subclass of a templated control needs its own ControlTheme or `StyleKeyOverride`.
3. Use only tokens (`DynamicResource` for `Brush*`/theme shadows, `StaticResource` for the rest),
   `{l:Tr ...}` for built-in text, `TemplateBinding` in templates. Mirror-safe (RTL) layout.
4. Visuals created in C# have no TemplatedParent: style them by class in `Components/ComponentStyles.axaml`.
5. Global styles beat ControlTheme styles: for state that must override a global button style, toggle a class on the button and style that class globally.
6. Clinic components stay display-only (plain text/enum properties), no business logic or Contracts DTOs.
7. Add a demo to the gallery and update `Docs/shared-components.md`.
